Q8. Compare MongoDB, Cassandra and Neo4j

```text
MongoDB

Data Model: Document Based
Storage Structure: BSON Documents
Query Method: MongoDB Query Language
Scalability: Horizontal and Vertical
Applications: Student Management, E-Commerce

Cassandra

Data Model: Column Family
Storage Structure: Rows and Columns
Query Method: Cassandra Query Language
Scalability: Horizontal
Applications: Banking, Big Data, IoT

Neo4j

Data Model: Graph Based
Storage Structure: Nodes and Relationships
Query Method: Cypher Query Language
Scalability: Distributed Graph Database
Applications: Social Networks, Recommendation Systems

Conclusion:

MongoDB is suitable for flexible document storage.
Cassandra is suitable for large distributed datasets.
Neo4j is suitable for relationship-based data.
```

